<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply rises to 16.6 pct on Apr 11.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply rises to 16.6 pct on Apr 11.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.6 percent on April 11, 1997, up from 15.6 percent on March 28, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Apr 11, 1997   Mar 28, 1997  Apr 12, 1996</p>
<p>		   16.6	     15.6	    15.8</p>
<p>Money supply was 7,107.83 billion rupees on April 11, 1997 against 6,990.52 billion on March 28, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
